I found an unresolved responder-side admission issue. The client selects an expected peer before SSH starts, but the fixed `ax rpc serve --stdio` command has no corresponding input that identifies which configured peer authenticated inbound. Selecting that peer from `hello.host_id` would let the untrusted claim choose its own comparison target.

I’ll document the evidence and routing options before adding an admission path that could give false assurance.

